On 12 Dec 2014 23:27, "Alex Burka" <aburka@seas.upenn.edu> wrote:
>
> I just realized you were probably using square brackets for IPA. So if I
understand correctly (relying on a Wikipedia chart here) [tuwitsku] would
be {tu uitsku}, gliding from the [u] to the [i], and [tu=CA=94itsku] is {tu
.itsku} with a pause/glottal stop in between. As I understand it Lojban is
of the opinion that [tuitsku] is indistinguishable from [tuwitsku].
>
> However, the debated ?{tuitsku} is pronounced [twitsku].

[w] is merely a necessarily-short subvariety of [u], and Lojban should not
be making phonological contrasts based on segment duration, because such
contrasts are not phonetically robust. That is, it's a bad idea for
[tuitsku] to be ambiguous between /tu witsku/ and /twitsku/, and that
ambiguity should be remedied and nullified by forbidding one of them. My
choice would be to forbid word-initial /w, y/, but since that's not an
option under consideration, it must be /twitsku/ that is declared illicit.

